{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1329150-aberrant-2e-character-sheet","id":1329150,"title":"Aberrant 2e Character Sheet","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-08-03T13:05:32-07:00","id":1329150,"title":"Aberrant 2e Character Sheet","content":"Being a neurotic ST for an Aberrant series I'm about to run, I put together a two page character sheet for the newest edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1PWv2NfVmy_7V_436BLYJnEXAdmzD70rZ/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1PWv2NfVmy_7V_436BLYJnEXAdmzD70rZ/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1PWv2NfVmy_7V_436BLYJnEXAdmzD70rZ/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/file/d/1PWv2NfVmy_7V_436BLYJnEXAdmzD70rZ/view?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1783,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1783-spanishinquisition","user":"SpanishInquisition","date":".  Updated edition. 08-07-2019, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1783-spanishinquisition","name":"SpanishInquisition","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1783_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-04T08:30:43-07:00","id":1329282,"title":"","content":"You have earned praise and laud.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-05T05:40:54-07:00","id":1329417,"title":"","content":"Yes, a very good sheet. I didn't think to overlay the Flux and the Transcendence together like perm/temp dots. Good Job there!<br /> <br /> Couple notes:<ul><li>Bruised as a +1 Modifier. I only see them for Injured and Maimed.</li> <li>I don;y think you need an &quot;Other Path&quot; because if you lose a Path you either regain the old one or replace it with a new one.</li> <li>Armor doesn't have a &quot;Base&quot; value. Merely just a collection of Tags. Though having just a Hard/Soft field is just fine. Maybe a place for other tags.</li> <li>The &quot;Enhancement&quot; section is a bit odd to me. Enhancement is a mechanical term. Are you thinking of &quot;Power Tags&quot; because Mega-Edges can have Power Tags</li> </ul><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2018-bioagent","name":"Bioagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-05T07:05:06-07:00","id":1329428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bioagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1329150-aberrant-2e-character-sheet?p=1329417#post1329417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]I don;y think you need an &amp;quot;Other Path&amp;quot; because if you lose a Path you either regain the old one or replace it with a new one.[*]Armor doesn't have a &amp;quot;Base&amp;quot; value. Merely just a collection of Tags. Though having just a Hard/Soft field is just fine. Maybe a place for other tags.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Just a few corrections here:<br /> You can have multiple paths, the book recommend not going above 5 because your character will not be able to keep all them active (as a person, not in the rules).<br /> By the rules (and some comments from devs) the base armour is 1 soft armor (that is not a tag, only one extra to the tags) and the soft tag add to it (that\u2019s what they meant by the minimum value of an armor is 1). The Durability and Quantum Field powers can have this base value higher them 1 (actually Q/2 round up). So a armor that just have the Soft 1 tag, actually have Soft Armor 2, and an armor with no tags have soft armor 1. That\u2019s what I understand from a few comments form devs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-06T05:11:54-07:00","id":1329603,"title":"","content":"Hmm, that needs to clarified. I know there is the rule for Armor rating, but it seems very counter-intuitive to all the armors in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2018-bioagent","name":"Bioagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-06T05:39:28-07:00","id":1329604,"title":"","content":"I can\u2019t find the line that talk about the number of paths, but in Core page 39, in the table it says \u201cAdd one dot in a new or existing Path (maximum five Paths)\u201d.<br /> <br /> This armor rating is more confusing than I wished, I honestly would be much more happy with the soft armor tag being the only source of soft armor (as you set in your house rules by the way, great simplification) and the tag staking up to 5 instead of only 1 or 2 (in the powers description fixed on 2).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-07T10:34:17-07:00","id":1329756,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the positive responses and feedback!<br /> <br /> Enhancements section is there to give my (mostly new) players a place to write down all the effects of their Mega Attribute and Mega Edges, so that they know what rolls to apply enhancements too - probably could have titled it ADVANTAGES or POWER EFFECTS. But I was trying to keep it as straight forward as possible.<br /> <br /> The quantum powers section, I tried to provide as much room for power tags as I could, but it was getting a little crowded. And power dilettantes may find themselves out of room.<br /> <br /> I left the Bruised health level off because you might have 4 Bruised levels, 4 Injured...etc...so I wanted to leave room to write in as many levels as the player needs. IE a stamina 3 PC can just write Bruised +1 above injured and ignore everything above and someone with Mega - Stamina can write in as many levels as they need.<br /> <br /> As for armor, the &quot;base&quot; isn't a number its a description - so bulletproof, impact, or slash-resistant - pg. 124. It confused me as well the first time I took a look at it.<br /> <br /> Edited link to 3 page edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1783,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1783-spanishinquisition","user":"SpanishInquisition","date":". 08-07-2019, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1783-spanishinquisition","name":"SpanishInquisition","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1783_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-13T17:25:52-07:00","id":1330863,"title":"","content":"Thanks for this. I made your character sheet form fill able so that its easier to make characters.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1TFoDmbtl5WUGliPB5oCoGZP4H9-hGVE3/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1TFoDmbtl5WUGliPB5oCoGZP4H9-hGVE3/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1TFoDmbtl5WUGliPB5oCoGZP4H9-hGVE3/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/file/d/1TFoDmbtl5WUGliPB5oCoGZP4H9-hGVE3/view?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25560-7thwiseguy","user":"7thwiseguy","date":".  Fixed form errors 08-17-2019, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25560-7thwiseguy","name":"7thwiseguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base6